values('PFQ-0001',1,'A community theatre plans a new ticketing service. The team records a proposed accessibility law, rising supplier prices and changing audience habits. Why would its manager group these findings using PESTLE?','[{"id":"a","text":"To turn the findings into a detailed task schedule."},{"id":"b","text":"To examine external influences that may change assumptions and decisions."},{"id":"c","text":"To allocate individual work packages to team members."},{"id":"d","text":"To confirm that every uncertainty is now controlled."}]'::jsonb,'b','PESTLE gives a structured view of external influences and their possible implications. A schedule and work allocation need further planning; recording a factor does not control it or remove uncertainty.')
