values('PFQ-0002',1,'A library’s self-service project assumes stable energy costs. An external review identifies a sustained price rise that could change the operating costs and the preferred option. What is the most useful management response?','[{"id":"a","text":"Keep the original operating-cost assumption because the project budget was approved."},{"id":"b","text":"Treat the external review as sufficient proof that the project should be cancelled."},{"id":"c","text":"Add more technical features to compensate without reviewing costs."},{"id":"d","text":"Assess the evidence, revisit the business-case assumptions and route any proposed change through the agreed decision process."}]'::jsonb,'d','Environmental scanning should inform decisions: test the evidence and reconsider the investment assumptions with the right decision makers. Approval does not make an assumption permanent; a finding alone neither proves cancellation is needed nor authorises extra scope.')
