values('PFQ-0003',1,'A regional organisation runs linked projects to introduce a shared booking service, train staff and change operating procedures. Their combined benefits depend on coordinated change. Which management approach fits this relationship?','[{"id":"a","text":"Programme management."},{"id":"b","text":"Managing each project independently with no shared coordination."},{"id":"c","text":"Business-as-usual supervision only."},{"id":"d","text":"Portfolio selection alone, without coordinating delivery."}]'::jsonb,'a','A programme coordinates related projects and change to realise benefits from their combined outcomes. A portfolio supports strategic investment choices, while business as usual operates continuing services. Independent delivery would not manage the stated interdependencies.')
