values('PFQ-0005',1,'A project manager reports that the forecast benefits no longer justify the remaining investment. Who would normally own the business case and sponsor the decision about continued viability?','[{"id":"a","text":"An external supplier acting alone."},{"id":"b","text":"The project sponsor."},{"id":"c","text":"Any end user who attended a demonstration."},{"id":"d","text":"The project management office, automatically for every project."}]'::jsonb,'b','The sponsor owns the business case and champions the investment and its benefits. The project manager provides information and manages delivery. Suppliers, users and a PMO can contribute evidence, but their participation does not automatically transfer sponsorship accountability.')
