values('PFQ-0006',1,'A project’s senior user, sponsor and manager disagree over an acceptance decision. Their responsibilities have never been agreed. Which response best addresses the underlying governance weakness?','[{"id":"a","text":"Let the manager accept on behalf of every stakeholder."},{"id":"b","text":"Ask the supplier to decide because it built the output."},{"id":"c","text":"Avoid documenting the decision until the disagreement disappears."},{"id":"d","text":"Clarify decision rights, responsibilities and escalation arrangements with the appropriate governance roles."}]'::jsonb,'d','Clear roles and governance establish who has authority and how disagreements are escalated. Neither managing delivery nor supplying an output automatically confers every acceptance right. Avoiding a record leaves the responsibility gap unresolved.')
on conflict(question_id) do update set content_version=excluded.content_version,stem=excluded.stem,choices=excluded.choices,correct_option_id=excluded.correct_option_id,explanation=excluded.explanation where current.content_version<=excluded.content_version;
