values('PFQ-0007',1,'A council is deciding whether to fund an archive digitisation project. Which information most directly helps its business case justify the investment?','[{"id":"a","text":"Options, expected benefits, costs, risks and the reasons for the preferred choice."},{"id":"b","text":"Only the names of the people attending the launch."},{"id":"c","text":"Only a list of completed technical tasks."},{"id":"d","text":"An unconditional promise that no assumptions will change."}]'::jsonb,'a','A business case explains why an investment is worthwhile by comparing options and considering benefits, costs, risks and assumptions. Attendance and task records cannot supply that justification, and uncertainty cannot be removed by promising it away.')
