values('PFQ-0008',1,'A new process has been handed over, but nobody is measuring the expected reduction in waiting time. What is missing from the benefits-management arrangements?','[{"id":"a","text":"A larger logo on the handover pack."},{"id":"b","text":"More detailed records of the developer’s working hours alone."},{"id":"c","text":"An accountable benefit owner and a plan to measure and review the outcome."},{"id":"d","text":"A rule that output delivery automatically proves every benefit."}]'::jsonb,'c','Benefits management needs responsibility for realising and measuring the intended improvement, including after handover. Delivering an output is distinct from obtaining a benefit. Branding or time records do not establish whether waiting times improved.')
