values('PFQ-0009',1,'A building conversion uses a planned sequence for structural work while a team develops the visitor app in short feedback cycles. How can the overall life cycle best be described?','[{"id":"a","text":"Extended, solely because more than one supplier is involved."},{"id":"b","text":"Hybrid, because it combines linear and iterative approaches."},{"id":"c","text":"Business as usual, because some tasks repeat."},{"id":"d","text":"Purely linear, because structural work exists."}]'::jsonb,'b','A hybrid life cycle combines linear and iterative approaches to suit the work. An extended life cycle includes attention to benefits beyond delivery; supplier count does not define it. Repeated development activities do not make a temporary change business as usual.')
