values('PFQ-0010',1,'A sponsor wants governance to consider whether the delivered equipment is actually adopted and produces the intended operational improvement, beyond the project’s delivery work. Which life-cycle concept best supports that wider view?','[{"id":"a","text":"Treating handover as proof that the benefits already exist."},{"id":"b","text":"Removing operational ownership so the manager owns benefits indefinitely."},{"id":"c","text":"Using iterations solely to avoid any transition work."},{"id":"d","text":"An extended project life cycle that includes benefits realisation beyond delivery."}]'::jsonb,'d','An extended life cycle connects delivery with adoption and benefits realisation. It does not make handover proof of success or remove operational ownership. Iterative delivery alone does not ensure the resulting change is adopted.')
