values('PFQ-0012',1,'A specialist produces a revised resource plan that shifts a key delivery date. What should happen before the project manager treats it as the agreed plan?','[{"id":"a","text":"Update the resource document alone and assume other plans will adjust themselves."},{"id":"b","text":"Hide the date change until the next handover."},{"id":"c","text":"Review the effect with relevant planning stakeholders and follow the agreed approval/change arrangements."},{"id":"d","text":"Ask only a person with no responsibility for the affected work."}]'::jsonb,'c','Integrated planning needs input from the stakeholders responsible for the affected work and decisions. A resource change can affect schedule, cost and other commitments. Isolated editing, concealment or irrelevant consultation cannot establish an agreed integrated plan.')
