values('PFQ-0013',1,'A project manager discovers that a small operations team can delay a vital handover even though it has few members. What should stakeholder analysis consider?','[{"id":"a","text":"Only how many people are in each team."},{"id":"b","text":"Only whether a stakeholder has attended a meeting."},{"id":"c","text":"Only the manager’s personal familiarity with the team."},{"id":"d","text":"The team’s interests, influence and relationship to the project decisions."}]'::jsonb,'d','Stakeholder analysis examines interests and influence, rather than using group size or attendance as a substitute. Understanding how the operations team affects handover helps the manager plan proportionate engagement.')
