values('PFQ-0014',1,'A regulator becomes more influential after a proposed operating rule changes. The team’s stakeholder analysis still places it in a low-influence group. What should the manager do?','[{"id":"a","text":"Keep the original category because analyses should never change."},{"id":"b","text":"Reassess the regulator’s influence and concerns, then adjust engagement responsibilities and activities."},{"id":"c","text":"Stop engaging all other stakeholders immediately."},{"id":"d","text":"Assume frequent generic newsletters will satisfy every new concern."}]'::jsonb,'b','Analysis needs revisiting as the project environment changes. Updated interests and influence should inform targeted engagement. Freezing categories, abandoning every other relationship or sending undifferentiated messages would not respond to the new situation.')
