values('PFQ-0017',1,'A supplier offers an unproven technique that might reduce delivery time, but success is uncertain. How should the possible favourable effect be understood?','[{"id":"a","text":"As an issue that has definitely occurred."},{"id":"b","text":"As proof the schedule can be shortened immediately."},{"id":"c","text":"As a reason to remove all existing risks."},{"id":"d","text":"As an opportunity to assess and manage as part of risk management."}]'::jsonb,'d','Risk concerns uncertainty that can affect objectives, including favourable opportunities. An uncertain advantage is not a confirmed outcome or a current issue. It needs assessment and an appropriate response rather than an automatic schedule change.')
