values('PFQ-0018',1,'A permit decision has already been delayed and is disrupting work. Further delays remain possible. How should the manager distinguish the immediate problem from the future uncertainty?','[{"id":"a","text":"Treat both only as completed benefits."},{"id":"b","text":"Manage the current disruption as an issue and assess the uncertain further delay as a risk."},{"id":"c","text":"Describe the current disruption only as a future risk so no action owner is needed."},{"id":"d","text":"Remove both from the records because they have the same cause."}]'::jsonb,'b','The disruption has happened and needs issue resolution; additional delay remains uncertain and needs risk assessment. A shared cause does not erase either management need. Labelling a current problem only as a future uncertainty can postpone necessary action.')
