values('PFQ-0022',1,'A client asks for a useful additional feature and offers to pay its direct development cost. The delivery date is fixed and testing uses scarce resources. What should the manager do before accepting?','[{"id":"a","text":"Accept immediately because direct development is funded."},{"id":"b","text":"Assess the wider scope, schedule, resource, quality and risk effects, then seek the required change decision."},{"id":"c","text":"Add it quietly if a developer is willing to work late."},{"id":"d","text":"Reject every request regardless of its value or impact."}]'::jsonb,'b','Change control considers integrated impact and appropriate authority, not just direct development cost. Testing capacity and the fixed date may affect feasibility. Quiet additions bypass control, while a blanket rejection avoids an informed decision.')
