values('PFQ-0024',1,'At concept stage, requirements and supplier conditions are uncertain. A director asks why the estimate is a range rather than a precise promise. Which explanation best reflects the estimating funnel?','[{"id":"a","text":"Early estimates are always exact if written as whole numbers."},{"id":"b","text":"The range must remain equally wide even after relevant evidence improves."},{"id":"c","text":"Limited early information supports a wider range; uncertainty can reduce as the work is defined and evidence improves."},{"id":"d","text":"The funnel eliminates every cost risk at the next meeting."}]'::jsonb,'c','The estimating funnel communicates uncertainty and increasing definition. A range can narrow with relevant evidence, but precision is not created by formatting and uncertainty is not guaranteed to disappear at a particular meeting.')
