values('PFQ-0025',1,'An activity’s total float is two days. If it slips by one day and the network assumptions remain valid, what does that normally mean for the project finish?','[{"id":"a","text":"The finish must slip by two days."},{"id":"b","text":"The activity no longer has any predecessors."},{"id":"c","text":"The manager can ignore its resource needs."},{"id":"d","text":"The finish need not move because the delay is within its total float."}]'::jsonb,'d','Total float is the time an activity can be delayed without delaying the project finish under the model’s assumptions. Using some float does not remove dependencies or resource constraints, and it does not necessarily delay completion.')
