values('PFQ-0028',1,'A board receives hundreds of unfiltered task updates but cannot see whether a key dependency threatens the next decision gate. How could reporting become more useful?','[{"id":"a","text":"Add more raw updates without explaining their relevance."},{"id":"b","text":"Suppress the dependency because it is uncomfortable to discuss."},{"id":"c","text":"Highlight the exception, its forecast effect, response and decision needed, supported by reliable source information."},{"id":"d","text":"Replace the forecast with an unsupported reassuring percentage."}]'::jsonb,'c','Useful reporting makes relevant performance, exceptions and required decisions clear, with supporting evidence. More volume is not automatically more useful. Hiding an issue or inventing a percentage prevents informed control.')
