values('PFQ-0029',1,'A newly formed project team understands its individual tasks but not why the project matters. Which leadership action most directly helps?','[{"id":"a","text":"Send a longer list of tasks without discussing the purpose."},{"id":"b","text":"Avoid questions until the project ends."},{"id":"c","text":"Make every decision without explaining the intended outcome."},{"id":"d","text":"Explain the shared purpose and help people connect their contributions to it."}]'::jsonb,'d','Leadership provides direction and helps people commit to a shared purpose. Task allocation can support management, but a larger task list alone does not explain why the project matters. Avoiding questions and unexplained decisions weaken that understanding.')
