values('PFQ-0030',1,'A dispersed team has different working hours and some members rarely speak in meetings. What is a proportionate approach to support collaboration?','[{"id":"a","text":"Assume silence proves agreement and use only one meeting time."},{"id":"b","text":"Agree accessible communication arrangements, invite contributions in different ways and check shared understanding."},{"id":"c","text":"Treat all differences as evidence that the team cannot work together."},{"id":"d","text":"Remove individual responsibility because collaboration is difficult."}]'::jsonb,'b','Effective teamwork accounts for how people can contribute and checks understanding. Agreed channels and inclusive participation help a dispersed team collaborate. Silence is not proof of agreement, and neither giving up nor removing responsibility addresses the communication barriers.')
